                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/1435: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-04T17:00:00-04:00">September 4, 1941—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>300. Your 418, September 3, 11 a.m. If you think it desirable, please express to
                    Rossetti on my behalf sincere appreciation for his indorsement of the principles
                    of continental solidarity for continental defense as set forth in his speech,
                    and described in your telegram under reference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
